& [SJS]
  + Situation: Slice3 returns proof-bound candidates but typed relation path structure lives only in human-readable contribution basis text and AnchorQueryResult lacks the canonical association_account field
  + Justification: lexical recall should not be added until existing exact and relation contributions can be audited as typed result accounts without reparsing prose
  + Solution: complete the result proof shape with closed typed relationship paths exact contribution-to-path validation and a fully recomputable per-channel association index

& [CompletedWorkSupportReview]
  + [completed_slice_id] Slice3ExactScanner
  + [proof_ref] C:\Project\Cantor\proofs\Cantor_Semantic_Anchor_Catalogue_P0_Slice3_Proof.sop
  + [support_delta] candidates already retain exact address channel basis value evidence guard and disposition data
  + [support_delta] relation traversal already holds ordered seed node relation type direction and hop data before formatting basis text
  + [support_delta] whole-result validation and digest recomputation are current
  + [requirement_gap] canonical relationship_path_set and association_account are not machine fields in AnchorQueryResult
  + [requirement_gap] no validator currently proves path chaining direction endpoint hop and evidence correspondence
  + [readiness_recompute] Slice4A is dependency-ready and does not require lexical scoring record content projection direct-query equivalence or provider access

& [Delineation]
  + machine representation and validation of already produced typed relation paths are inside
  + deterministic grouping of existing contributions by their unchanged channels is inside
  + relationship path and association account digest commitment is inside
  + lexical proposal generation compact semantic detail projection and direct-query comparison are outside
  + path identity records navigation evidence and never creates a semantic relation
  + association account is an index over contribution records and never combines their local value domains

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + [conceptual_model] relationship direction step path contribution channel account query result
  + [logical_model] traversal emits one typed path contribution validator proves chain result derives path set and channel groups then digest commits all
  + [physical_model] closed Rust enums structs sorted vectors BTree sets and canonical serde JSON
  + [source_data] already validated SemanticRelation traversal state candidate contributions and exact SemanticAddress values
  + [derived_projection] relationship_paths and association_account inside AnchorQueryResult
  + [freshness_rule] any candidate contribution step channel path account or ordering mutation changes digest or refuses
  + [recompute_rule] rebuild both accounts from candidates and never patch them independently
  + [authoritative_store] admitted packages and exact candidate contributions
  + [derived_store] result-local indexes only

& [OperatorContract]
  + [input] one candidate set whose contributions already passed Slice3 exact scanner gates
  + [output] canonical typed paths and per-channel association accounts committed in AnchorQueryResult
  + [precondition] every typed relation contribution has a path and every non-relation contribution lacks one
  + [postcondition] result paths and accounts exactly equal deterministic derivation from candidates
  + [failure_behavior] closed AnchorFormFault without repaired or partial output
  + [side_effect] none

& [FeatureRequirementSupport]
  + [SAC4A-001] define closed direction step path and channel-account forms; support gap is implementation
  + [SAC4A-002] bind typed relation contribution path to candidate hop evidence chain and direction; support prepared by traversal state
  + [SAC4A-003] derive canonical result relationship path set from contributions; support gap is projection helper and validator
  + [SAC4A-004] derive canonical channel account from all candidate contributions; support gap is projection helper and validator
  + [SAC4A-005] commit new fields under result digest and whole-result rebuild; support prepared by existing digest and scanner verifier
  + [SAC4A-006] prove wrong channel chain endpoint hop evidence ordering duplication omission extra and digest mutations fail closed; support gap is focused tests
  + [SAC4A-007] preserve lexical provider effect and rollback boundaries; support prepared by additive forms and full regression
  + [slice_readiness] ready_after_phase_lock

& [DualHemisphereReview]
  + Master view: a graph walk should remain visible as an actual walked relationship rather than collapse into a sentence claiming that a relationship occurred
  + Emissary view: direction enum exact endpoints typed steps hop equality evidence closure canonical order and recomputed accounts make the walk executable and testable
  + correction: adding lexical recall first would multiply contribution channels while the result still lacks a complete association ledger
  + reconciliation: complete the ledger and path grammar first then let later recall channels enter the same inspected structure

& [Premortem]
  + failure: basis prose and typed path disagree; cause dual manual construction; mitigation construct both from one traversal state and validate typed path independently
  + failure: reverse traversal lies about direction; cause endpoint inference error; mitigation direction must agree with source-target orientation of the exact relation
  + failure: account omits excluded or incompatible contribution; cause counting retained only; mitigation account all contribution records by declared channel and exact candidate IDs
  + failure: duplicate paths pass through multiple candidates; cause noncanonical aggregation; mitigation strict sort unique and exact recomputation
  + failure: form change breaks old fixtures silently; cause missing digest fields; mitigation compile failures focused mutations and full workspace regression
  + failure: Slice4A starts lexical behavior; cause convenient refactor expansion; mitigation hard source boundary and no tokenizer scorer or new proposal entry point

& [SevenFoldTrace]
  + fold_1 consumes published Slice3 proof and preserves a new sub-slice source
  + fold_2 separates relationship evidence from natural-language explanation and association indexing from scoring
  + fold_3 models direction step path channel account and result closure
  + fold_4 traces each proposed field to existing traversal and contribution data
  + fold_5 prunes lexical projection provider persistence effect remote and Minecraft behavior
  + fold_6 adds chain direction hop evidence account ordering duplication and digest adversarial tests
  + fold_7 converges on closed forms pure derivation validators scanner population and no new discovery behavior
  + [gain_delta] every relation proposal and channel grouping becomes inspectable machine data before the proposal surface expands
  + [exhaustion_state] phase_locked_for_Slice4A_implementation

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty requires the typed path to agree with basis candidate evidence direction and hop claims
  + Security requires closed fields canonical order exact recomputation and digest commitment
  + Weaver supplies path composition but receives no authority from the association account
  + Planner orders steps and channels without mixing their local values
  + Refiner derives one minimal path set and one minimal channel index without duplicating record bodies
  + Scribe records every step endpoint channel candidate and count
  + Observer compares the complete result fields to their candidate-derived canonical rebuild

& [Decision]
  + activate Slice4A result path and association-account forms validators scanner population and focused tests only
  + allow no lexical compact record projection direct-query equivalence embedding learned provider persistence remote hidden-state effect FPGA or Minecraft implementation
  + require solution proof narrative attribution full workspace verification lint format and evidence refresh before completion

